+TASK — Phase 2 only: Database schema.
+
+1. Set up Prisma in the backend (install prisma and @prisma/client, initialize it).
+2. Create the complete schema.prisma file with these models and proper relations:
+
+- User: id, phoneNumber (unique), email (optional, unique), passwordHash, name, avatarUrl, statusMessage, isOnline, lastSeenAt, createdAt, updatedAt
+- Contact: id, ownerId (User), contactUserId (User), createdAt
+- Conversation: id, isGroup (boolean), groupName (optional), groupAvatarUrl (optional), createdAt, updatedAt
+- ConversationParticipant: id, conversationId, userId, role (enum: MEMBER, ADMIN), joinedAt, isMuted, isArchived
+- Message: id, conversationId, senderId, content (optional, for text), messageType (enum: TEXT, IMAGE, VIDEO, AUDIO, DOCUMENT), replyToMessageId (optional, self-relation), isEdited, isDeletedForEveryone, createdAt, updatedAt
+- MessageStatus: id, messageId, userId, status (enum: SENT, DELIVERED, READ), updatedAt
+- MessageReaction: id, messageId, userId, emoji, createdAt
+- MediaAttachment: id, messageId, url, mimeType, sizeBytes, durationSeconds (optional, for audio/video)
+
+3. Add appropriate @@unique, @@index, and onDelete behavior where sensible (e.g. cascade delete messages when a conversation is deleted).
+4. Do not write any actual API routes or business logic yet — schema only.
+5. After creating schema.prisma, run `npx prisma generate` to confirm it's valid, and show me the output.
+
+Do not attempt to run migrations yet — I need to add my real database connection string first.

