# 2026-07-22 09:07:44.853567
+We are continuing the WhatsApp-clone chat app project. Phase 1 (folder structure) and Phase 2 (Prisma schema + migration) are complete and working.
+
+TASK — Phase 3 only: Authentication.
+
+1. Install needed backend packages: bcrypt, jsonwebtoken, zod, and their @types dev packages.
+2. Create src/services/auth.service.ts with functions: hashPassword, comparePassword, generateAccessToken, generateRefreshToken, verifyAccessToken, verifyRefreshToken. Use JWT_SECRET and JWT_REFRESH_SECRET from process.env. Access token expires in 15m, refresh token in 7d.
+3. Create src/controllers/auth.controller.ts with handlers: signup, login, refreshToken, logout.
+   - signup: accepts phoneNumber, name, password. Validates with zod. Checks phoneNumber isn't already taken. Hashes password. Creates user. Returns access + refresh tokens.
+   - login: accepts phoneNumber, password. Validates with zod. Verifies user exists and password matches. Returns access + refresh tokens.
+   - refreshToken: accepts a refresh token, verifies it, issues a new access token.
+   - logout: stateless for now, just returns success (we'll add token blacklisting later if needed).
+4. Create src/middleware/auth.middleware.ts — an Express middleware that reads the Authorization: Bearer <token> header, verifies the access token, and attaches the decoded user id to req.userId. Returns 401 if missing or invalid.
+5. Create src/routes/auth.routes.ts with POST /signup, POST /login, POST /refresh, POST /logout, wired to the controller functions.
+6. Wire the auth routes into src/index.ts under the path /api/auth.
+7. Do not build any other routes yet (users, contacts, conversations) — only auth in this phase.
+
+After creating everything, show me the final file list.

