# 2026-07-22 12:09:58.952247
+We are continuing the WhatsApp-clone chat app project. Phase 1 (structure), Phase 2 (database schema), and Phase 3 (authentication) are complete and tested working.
+
+Important: reuse the existing authMiddleware from src/middleware/auth.middleware.ts (exported as authMiddleware) on every route below except none are public — all these routes require a logged-in user. It attaches req.userId (a number) to the request.
+
+TASK — Phase 4 only: Users, Contacts, and Conversations REST APIs.
+
+1. Create src/controllers/user.controller.ts:
+   - getMe: returns the logged-in user's own profile (id, phoneNumber, email, name, avatarUrl, statusMessage, isOnline, lastSeenAt) using req.userId. Never return passwordHash.
+   - updateMe: accepts optional name, avatarUrl, statusMessage in the body, validates with zod, updates the logged-in user, returns the updated profile (no passwordHash).
+   - searchUsers: accepts a query param "phoneNumber", finds a user by exact phone number match (excluding the requester), returns basic public info (id, name, phoneNumber, avatarUrl) or 404 if not found.
+
+2. Create src/controllers/contact.controller.ts:
+   - addContact: accepts contactUserId in the body, creates a Contact row linking req.userId as owner to that user, returns the created contact with the contact user's basic info included. Handle duplicate contact gracefully (409 if already exists).
+   - listContacts: returns all contacts for req.userId, including each contact user's basic info (id, name, phoneNumber, avatarUrl, isOnline, lastSeenAt).
+   - removeContact: accepts contactUserId as a URL param, deletes that contact for req.userId.
+
+3. Create src/controllers/conversation.controller.ts:
+   - createConversation: accepts participantUserIds (array of user ids) and optional isGroup, groupName. If isGroup is false or omitted and there's already a 1:1 conversation between the two users, return that existing conversation instead of creating a duplicate. Creates the Conversation and ConversationParticipant rows (creator gets ADMIN role if isGroup, MEMBER otherwise). Returns the created/found conversation with participants included.
+   - listConversations: returns all conversations req.userId participates in, ordered by most recent message activity, including participants' basic info and the last message (if any) as a preview. Paginate with a "cursor" and "limit" query param (default limit 20).
+   - getConversationMessages: accepts conversationId as a URL param, verifies req.userId is a participant (403 if not), returns messages for that conversation ordered newest-first, paginated with "cursor" and "limit" query params (default limit 30). Include sender basic info and any message statuses relevant to req.userId.
+
+4. Create src/routes/user.routes.ts, src/routes/contact.routes.ts, src/routes/conversation.routes.ts wiring these controllers with authMiddleware applied to every route.
+
+5. Wire these new route files into src/index.ts under /api/users, /api/contacts, /api/conversations respectively.
+
+6. Use zod for input validation on every endpoint that accepts a body or meaningful params. Wrap all database logic in try/catch and return appropriate status codes (400 for validation errors, 404 for not found, 403 for forbidden, 409 for conflict, 500 for unexpected errors) with a { message: string } JSON body — never leak raw error objects or passwordHash to the client.
+
+Do not implement Socket.IO / real-time messaging yet — that's Phase 5. This phase is REST APIs only, backed by the existing Prisma models.
+
+After creating everything, show me the final file list.

