# 2026-07-22 13:35:48.077083
+We are continuing the WhatsApp-clone chat app project. Phases 1-4 are complete and tested working: folder structure, Prisma schema, authentication (JWT), and REST APIs for users/contacts/conversations.
+
+Important context:
+- The Express app and HTTP server are created in src/index.ts.
+- authMiddleware (from src/middleware/auth.middleware.ts) verifies JWT access tokens from the Authorization header for REST routes.
+- Prisma models: User, Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageStatus, MessageReaction, MediaAttachment (see prisma/schema.prisma for exact field names — do not guess field names, use exactly what's in the schema).
+
+TASK — Phase 5 only: Socket.IO real-time layer.
+
+1. Install socket.io on the backend if not already present (it's already in package.json, just make sure it's installed).
+
+2. Create src/sockets/socket.auth.ts: a Socket.IO middleware function that reads the JWT access token from the connection handshake (socket.handshake.auth.token), verifies it using the existing verifyAccessToken function from auth.service.ts, and attaches the decoded userId to socket.data.userId. If verification fails, reject the connection with an error.
+
+3. Create src/sockets/socket.handlers.ts with a function `registerSocketHandlers(io: Server)` that sets up:
+   - On connection: mark the user online in the database (isOnline: true), join the socket to a room named `user:<userId>` for direct targeting, and join rooms for every conversation the user participates in (room name `conversation:<conversationId>`).
+   - Event "message:send": accepts { conversationId, content, messageType, replyToMessageId }. Verifies the sender is a participant in that conversation. Creates the Message in the database. Emits "message:new" with the full message (including sender info) to everyone in the `conversation:<conversationId>` room, including the sender.
+   - Event "typing:start": accepts { conversationId }. Broadcasts "typing:update" with { conversationId, userId, isTyping: true } to everyone else in that conversation room (not back to the sender).
+   - Event "typing:stop": same as above but isTyping: false.
+   - Event "message:delivered": accepts { messageId }. Creates or updates a MessageStatus row for that message and the current user with status DELIVERED. Emits "message:status" with { messageId, userId, status: 'DELIVERED' } to the conversation room.
+   - Event "message:read": same pattern as delivered but status READ.
+   - On disconnect: mark the user offline (isOnline: false) and set lastSeenAt to now. Emit "presence:update" with { userId, isOnline: false, lastSeenAt } to all conversation rooms the user was part of.
+
+4. In src/index.ts, create the Socket.IO server attached to the existing HTTP server, apply the socket.auth middleware, and call registerSocketHandlers(io). Make sure CORS is configured to allow the frontend origin from CLIENT_URL in .env.
+
+5. Wrap all database operations in try/catch. If an operation fails, emit an "error" event back to that specific socket with a message, don't crash the connection.
+
+Do not build any frontend code yet — backend Socket.IO only, this phase.
+
+After creating everything, show me the final file list.

