+We are continuing the WhatsApp-clone chat app project. The backend is fully working: authentication (JWT), REST APIs for users/contacts/conversations, and Socket.IO real-time messaging (events: message:send, message:new, typing:start, typing:stop, typing:update, message:delivered, message:read, message:status, presence:update).
+
+Backend base URL: http://localhost:3000
+Backend REST routes:
+- POST /api/auth/signup { phoneNumber, name, password } -> { user, accessToken, refreshToken }
+- POST /api/auth/login { phoneNumber, password } -> { user, accessToken, refreshToken }
+- POST /api/auth/refresh { refreshToken } -> { accessToken }
+- GET /api/users/me (auth required) -> user profile
+- GET /api/contacts (auth required) -> list of contacts
+- POST /api/contacts { contactUserId } (auth required)
+- POST /api/conversations/create { participantUserIds, isGroup?, groupName? } (auth required)
+- GET /api/conversations (auth required, query: cursor, limit) -> { conversations, nextCursor }
+- GET /api/conversations/:conversationId/messages (auth required, query: cursor, limit) -> { messages, nextCursor }
+
+All authenticated REST requests need header: Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
+Socket.IO connection needs: io(url, { auth: { token: accessToken } })
+
+The frontend project already exists at frontend/ with Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind configured (from Phase 1). Folders exist: src/components, src/pages, src/hooks, src/store, src/lib, src/types.
+
+TASK — Phase 7a only: Auth screens + API client setup. Do not build the chat UI yet.
+
+1. Install axios, socket.io-client, zustand, react-router-dom in the frontend.
+
+2. Create src/lib/api.ts: an axios instance with baseURL from import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL (fallback http://localhost:3000/api), an interceptor that attaches the Authorization header from the auth store's accessToken, and a response interceptor that on 401 tries POST /auth/refresh once using the stored refreshToken, then retries the original request; if refresh also fails, clear the auth store and redirect to /login.
+
+3. Create src/store/authStore.ts using zustand: state { user, accessToken, refreshToken, isAuthenticated }, actions { login(user, accessToken, refreshToken), logout() }, persisted to localStorage using zustand's persist middleware.
+
+4. Create src/types/auth.ts with TypeScript interfaces: User { id, phoneNumber, name, email, avatarUrl, statusMessage, isOnline, lastSeenAt }, AuthResponse { user, accessToken, refreshToken }.
+
+5. Create src/pages/LoginPage.tsx: a form with phoneNumber and password fields, calls POST /auth/login via the api client, on success calls authStore.login(...) and navigates to "/". Show validation errors and a loading state. Style with Tailwind, clean centered card layout.
+
+6. Create src/pages/SignupPage.tsx: same pattern but phoneNumber, name, password fields, calls POST /auth/signup.
+
+7. Create src/App.tsx with react-router-dom routing: "/login" -> LoginPage, "/signup" -> SignupPage, "/" -> a placeholder "Home" page that just shows "Logged in as {user.name}" with a logout button (we'll replace this with the real chat UI in the next phase). Add a simple ProtectedRoute wrapper that redirects to /login if not authenticated.
+
+8. Update src/main.tsx to wrap App with BrowserRouter if not already done by react-router-dom setup conventions.
+
+Use Tailwind utility classes for all styling — clean, modern, WhatsApp-inspired color scheme (greens/teals), centered forms, rounded corners, subtle shadows.
+
+After creating everything, show me the final file list.

