# 2026-07-23 09:40:40.238267
+We are continuing the WhatsApp-clone chat app project. Backend (auth, REST APIs, Socket.IO) and frontend auth screens are complete and tested working.
+
+Existing frontend files you should reuse, not recreate:
+- src/lib/api.ts (axios instance with Authorization header + token refresh)
+- src/store/authStore.ts (zustand store: user, accessToken, refreshToken, isAuthenticated, login(), logout())
+- src/types/auth.ts (User, AuthResponse interfaces)
+- src/App.tsx (has ProtectedRoute wrapper and routing — you will modify this to add new routes/replace HomePage)
+
+Backend REST routes available (baseURL already configured in api.ts, so just use relative paths like '/contacts'):
+- GET /users/me -> current user profile
+- GET /contacts -> array of { id, name, phoneNumber, avatarUrl, isOnline, lastSeenAt }
+- POST /contacts { contactUserId } -> add a contact
+- POST /conversations/create { participantUserIds: number[], isGroup?, groupName? } -> conversation object
+- GET /conversations?cursor&limit -> { conversations: [{ id, isGroup, groupName, participants: [{id, name, phoneNumber, avatarUrl, isOnline, lastSeenAt}], lastMessage: {id, content, senderId, createdAt} | null }], nextCursor }
+- GET /conversations/:conversationId/messages?cursor&limit -> { messages: [{ id, content, senderId, senderName, senderAvatarUrl, createdAt }], nextCursor }
+
+Socket.IO events (connect with: io('http://localhost:3000', { auth: { token: accessToken } })):
+- Emit "message:send" { conversationId, content, messageType: 'TEXT', replyToMessageId: null }, with an ack callback receiving { message } or { error }
+- Listen "message:new" -> full message object { id, conversationId, senderId, content, messageType, createdAt, sender: {id, name, avatarUrl} }
+- Emit "typing:start" { conversationId } and "typing:stop" { conversationId }
+- Listen "typing:update" -> { conversationId, userId, isTyping }
+- Listen "presence:update" -> { userId, isOnline, lastSeenAt }
+
+TASK — Phase 7b: Chat UI.
+
+1. Create src/hooks/useSocket.ts: a custom hook that creates a single socket.io-client connection using the accessToken from authStore, connects on mount, disconnects on unmount, and returns the socket instance (or null before connected). Reuse the same socket instance across the app (don't reconnect on every component render — use a ref or module-level singleton pattern).
+
+2. Create src/store/chatStore.ts using zustand: state for conversations (array), activeConversationId (number | null), messages (a Record<conversationId, Message[]>), typingUsers (a Record<conversationId, number[]> of userIds currently typing). Actions: setConversations, setActiveConversation, addMessage(conversationId, message) [prepend/append correctly, avoid duplicates by message id], setMessages(conversationId, messages), setUserTyping(conversationId, userId, isTyping), updateConversationLastMessage.
+
+3. Create src/types/chat.ts with interfaces: Contact, Conversation, Message, matching the backend response shapes described above.
+
+4. Create src/components/Sidebar.tsx: fetches conversations via GET /conversations on mount, lists them (avatar placeholder circle with first letter of name if no avatarUrl, name or group name, last message preview truncated, relative timestamp), clicking one sets it as active conversation and navigates to /chat/:conversationId. Include a simple "New Chat" button that prompts for a phone number, looks up nothing fancy — just calls POST /contacts is not needed here, instead directly try creating a conversation: ask for a phone number via a simple modal/prompt, then you'll need a way to find the user by phone number first. Add a small inline search using a phone number input, calling GET /users/search?phoneNumber=... if needed — if this endpoint doesn't exist yet, just build the UI assuming a function findUserByPhone(phoneNumber) exists in src/lib/api.ts that hits GET /users/search?phoneNumber= (create this function, we'll make sure the backend route matches).
+
+5. Create src/components/ChatWindow.tsx: shown when a conversation is active. Fetches message history via GET /conversations/:id/messages on mount/conversation change. Renders messages as bubbles (sender's own messages right-aligned in emerald, others left-aligned in dark gray), each with timestamp. Auto-scrolls to bottom on new message. Has a text input + send button at the bottom; pressing Enter or clicking send emits "message:send" via the socket, optimistically adds the message to chatStore, and clears the input. Shows a typing indicator ("... is typing") when typingUsers has entries for this conversation. Emits "typing:start" on input change (debounced) and "typing:stop" after 2 seconds of no typing or on send.
+
+6. Create src/pages/ChatPage.tsx: the main authenticated layout — Sidebar on the left (fixed width, full height), ChatWindow on the right (flex-grow), dark theme matching the login/signup pages (black background, emerald/teal accents). If no conversation is selected, show a placeholder "Select a conversation to start chatting" in the empty right panel.
+
+7. Update src/App.tsx: replace the placeholder HomePage with ChatPage at route "/", wrapped in ProtectedRoute. Add route "/chat/:conversationId" also rendering ChatPage (it should read the conversationId from useParams and set it as active).
+
+8. Wire useSocket into ChatPage (or a top-level provider) so the socket connects once when the user is authenticated, and listen for "message:new" (call chatStore.addMessage + updateConversationLastMessage), "typing:update" (call chatStore.setUserTyping), globally for the whole authenticated app, not just within ChatWindow, so messages arrive even if you're viewing a different conversation.
+
+Use Tailwind, dark theme (black/dark gray backgrounds, emerald-500/teal-500 accents, matching the login page style). Keep components reasonably sized and readable.
+
+Do not implement group chat creation, reactions, reply, edit, delete, or media upload yet — those are later phases. Just core 1:1 text messaging with real-time updates, typing indicators, and online status display.
+
+After creating everything, show me the final file list.

